# Source preparation pipeline to be run from mapterhorn/pipelines folder.
# Two N41/N42 x E140 1-degree Copernicus GLO-30 tiles covering the
# Hakodate/Goryokaku trial area and its surrounding sea -- a low-priority
# global fallback (maxzoom forced down to macrotile_z=12 by
# aggregation_covering.py, well below the 1m/5m/10m trial sources' 17,
# so it can never win their equal-maxzoom tie-break) so that open ocean
# renders as real (near-0m) elevation instead of nodata. Mirrors how
# upstream Mapterhorn's own published data blends sea in -- see
# mapterhorn-japan-bridge's DECISIONS.md D11 for the investigation that
# led here. Filtered from the full source-catalog/glo30 (24,674 global
# tiles) rather than reusing that entry directly, so a bridge run never
# accidentally pulls the whole planet.
[no-cd]
default:
    uv run python source_download.py jphakodatetrialsea
    uv run python source_bounds.py jphakodatetrialsea
    uv run python source_polygonize.py jphakodatetrialsea 4
